  "questions": [
    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-49003",
      "knowledge_point_id": "a67f347a-30a5-5169-af2c-9a800be84e46",
      "knowledge_point": "Determining Concavity and the Sign of the Derivative at a Point",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041640/assets/03b4d6fea89eb695e0919aed4a82b1d25ff5e296338381192b5236f5295bef12.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. For which of the following values of $x$ is $f(x)$ concave up *and* ${f}^{′}(x)<0?$",
      "worked_solution": "We begin by noticing that at $x=b$ the graph has a corner point, which implies that the derivative doesn't exist there.\n\nThe derivative ${f}^{′}(x)$ is negative when $f(x)$ is decreasing. From the given graph, we see that only $x=c$ and $x=e$ are on decreasing parts of the graph.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14041640/assets/f33639f6a54a2e0f35c52b684356ed832047ee538b8651e9ca9f75a542d366a9.png)\n\nThe concavity of a function refers to the direction in which its graph curves.\n\n- If the graph curves upward, like a \"smile\" ($⌣$), then the graph is said to be *concave up*.\n\n- If the graph curves downward, like a \"frown\" ($⌢$), then the graph is said to be *concave down*.\n\nIt's helpful to remember the mnemonic \"concave down like a frown.\"\n\nOf the points $x=c$ and $x=e,$ the graph is concave up ($⌣$) at $x=c$ only.",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x=e"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x=b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x=c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x=a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "x=d"
            }
          ],
          "correct_value": "x=c",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "correct_origin": "ma_successful_grade"
        }
      ],
      "knowledge_point_source_id": 10003,
      "difficulty": "moderate",
